From 8603acbbbce6c8df9b64f56df75a2c359b4eded5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mrfelek <17274927+mrfelek@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 17:38:21 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(shader): fold descriptor web paths that hold the lane
 index or texels

A descriptor web path whose T# dwords are per-lane values left in the
registers (the lane index from v_mbcnt or arithmetic of texels from an
image read) was not rebuilt and the read stopped with "GetImageResource
dword 0 is not a valid runtime value". PPSA26344 compute shader
0x800037fe00 has such a path into its waterfall loop.

Fold these paths like the program counter, EXEC and lane mask ones:
select the first descriptor and record an InvalidDescriptor fault when
a lane takes the path. APS5_STRICT_DESCRIPTOR_WEBS still throws.

Folding exposed per-lane selections taken in the wrong order: when a
tuple held selects from two blocks, the first one found became the
outer selector even if it sat in the dominating block, so the inner
selector placed in the later block did not dominate its use. Take the
select in the latest block first.

AI-assisted. Tested by me on my own machine.
